R_X &\lesssim \$2\,\mathrm{M}.\end{aligned}$ Here $C_X$ is the likely investment check and $R_X$ is company revenue. The point is stage fit. A very early round in this interview does not necessarily mean no revenue; it can mean a company with some operating reality but still below about $\$2\,\mathrm{M}$ in revenue.

