The case is a construction loan on a business the speaker says he really did not want to be in. He was talked into it by a friend. The loan was supposed to be temporary, and everything was collateralized. On paper, those words are meant to make exposure look bounded: $E_{\mathrm{nominal}}
=
E_{\mathrm{capital\ under\ loan\ terms}}.$ But the transcript’s lesson is that the nominal exposure was not the total exposure. The company ended up with failing management, and the speaker says he had to step in and spend a couple of years turning it around.

