This section should not be read as a claim that every collateralized loan is dangerous. The doctrine is narrower. Before accepting a deal, the founder or financier should ask what role the downside could force him to occupy. In symbols: $\text{reject the deal if}
\qquad
E_{\mathrm{total}}>W_{\mathrm{own}},$ where $W_{\mathrm{own}}$ is the real willingness to own the problem if the optimistic description fails. Lecture 115’s point is that the speaker already knew the answer from day one. He did not want to be in that business, but proceeded anyway.

